# SRG-APP-000086-AU-000390  -  CAT II
# Where multiple log servers are installed in the enclave, each log server
# must be configured to aggregate log records to a central aggregation
# server or other consolidated events repository.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000086-AU-000390
group:           V-206451
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      tested
cci:             CCI-000174
control_rev5:    AU-12

contribution:    Where this instance is one of several log servers, Splunk can forward
                 everything it receives to the central aggregation server: a
                 [tcpout:<target_group>] stanza carries the aggregator's host and port in
                 'server', the top-level 'defaultGroup' selects that group so all data is
                 sent, and indexAndForward keeps a local copy in addition on a heavy
                 forwarder.

governs:         outputs.conf - Where this instance forwards its data, and how that connection is
                 protected.

check:           outputs.conf [tcpout] defaultGroup non_empty
check:           outputs.conf [tcpout:<target_group>] server non_empty
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          outputs.conf [tcpout:<target_group>] server https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/outputs.conf
vendor:          outputs.conf [tcpout] defaultGroup https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/forward-and-process-data/forwarding-and-receiving-data/10.4/configure-forwarders/configure-forwarding-with-outputs.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Whether the enclave holds multiple log servers, and therefore whether this
                 requirement applies at all, is read from the network architecture
                 documentation. The application cannot determine its own place in the
                 topology, and a single-log-server site is not a finding against it.
external:        Existence and acceptance of the central aggregation server, SIEM or
                 consolidated events repository, which is a separate system.
external:        Transport protection for the forwarded records, configured in the
                 outputs.conf SSL settings and assessed under the SC requirements.

citation:        SRG-APP-000086-AU-000390 check text; SPLK-CL-000110 check and fix text;
                 outputs.conf.spec:61-70 ([tcpout], defaultGroup = <comma-separated list>);
                 outputs.conf.spec:72-79 (indexAndForward = <boolean>, Default: false);
                 outputs.conf.spec:118-130 ([tcpout:<target_group>], server =
                 <comma-separated list>)
finding:         Where this instance is one of multiple log servers, Splunk Enterprise has
                 no outputs.conf target group naming the central aggregation server, or no
                 defaultGroup selecting it, so the records it receives are not forwarded to
                 the consolidated repository.
